# Line-ending rules.
#
# Only shell scripts are pinned here, and deliberately so: a global
# "* text=auto eol=lf" would renormalise every text file in the repository and
# produce an enormous unrelated diff. The .blend pack is binary and is already
# detected as such, so leaving the rest to git's defaults is correct.

# A hook or script committed with CRLF endings fails on every platform with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M". core.autocrlf is commonly true on
# Windows, so pin these to LF in the repository rather than relying on each
# contributor's local git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
.github/hooks/pre-push text eol=lf
